                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 74-year-old female, admitted on 05/08/1956 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, physical examination, laboratory investigations, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed acute appendicitis without evidence of perforation. Given her age and clinical presentation, an emergency appendectomy was performed promptly under general anaesthesia. The intraoperative findings were consistent with acute non-perforated appendicitis. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound healing was satisfactory, and the patient mobilised well with physiotherapy support. Appropriate analgesia and intravenous fluids were administered perioperatively. She was discharged in stable condition on 06/08/1956 with wound care instructions and follow-up recommendations. Please do not hesitate to contact me should any questions arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
